cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Recognition Kernel"
message: "If you use this software or specification, please cite both the software and the paper it implements."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Koepsell
    given-names: David R.
    email: drkoepsell@tamu.edu
    affiliation: "SEAL Lab, Texas A&M University"
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A reference implementation of a domain-neutral kernel of twelve contradiction
  primitives in four strata, indexed over the seven links of a recognition chain.
  Ships a formal specification (OWL 2 DL, JSON Schema, prose, worked examples),
  a rule-based norm and chain extractor with a K-D3 detector, and a domain
  typology generator that returns the full typology, the gated profile, and the
  predicted failure modes for any domain chain.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "The Recognition Layer: A Generative Typology of Structural Contradiction for Recognition-Constituted Domains"
    authors:
      - family-names: Koepsell
        given-names: David R.
    notes: "Working draft. The specification in spec/SPEC.md implements sections 5 through 8."
